const JUDGE_FAIR = "BE FAIR, NOT PICKY. Judge it against what it is meant to be - the request and the builder's own plan - never against your own taste. If it already looks good and matches its plan, it is OK: say ok true with no problems. Report only clear, real mistakes anyone would notice at a glance: torn, broken or see-through skin, holes, parts floating, detached, poking through or plainly in the wrong place, something the request or the plan asks for that is missing, or a body that is obviously crude for a finished character. Never report matters of taste or style, small imperfections, things you are unsure about, or could-be-even-better improvements, and never ask for more detail on something that already looks finished - a needless rebuild makes it worse, not better. A body built from plain, basic shapes (simple spheres, boxes and capsules with no real form), parts that do not touch what they belong to, or a character clearly far below the finished main cast in detail, finish and organic shaping IS broken - never a nitpick. Mark every problem with a severity: broken (a real mistake that must be fixed) or minor (a nitpick - minor ones are ignored, so only use broken when it truly is). Never report the pictures themselves (framing, crop, camera angle, lighting, background) as a problem - only the character. If the pictures show no character at all (just an empty background), that is a rendering problem, not a mistake in the character: return ok true with no problems and not_visible true.";
